WEBVTT

1
00:00:29.833 --> 00:00:31.666
<b>The previous verse explained</b>

2
00:00:31.666 --> 00:00:37.333
<b>that those who don't follow Krishna's teachings </b>
<b>are heading toward destruction.</b>

3
00:00:37.333 --> 00:00:39.166
<b>But if this is true,</b>

4
00:00:39.166 --> 00:00:43.833
<b>why doesn't everyone fully</b>
<b>follow these teachings?</b>

5
00:00:43.833 --> 00:00:47.333
<b>Why do people disregard them?</b>

6
00:00:47.333 --> 00:00:50.750
<b>This verse answers these questions.</b>

7
00:00:55.625 --> 00:01:00.500
<b>Human beings operate according to the </b>
<b>qualities they receive from material nature,</b>

8
00:01:00.500 --> 00:01:03.416
<b>and act accordingly.</b>

9
00:01:03.416 --> 00:01:05.000
<b>Every person is unique,</b>

10
00:01:05.000 --> 00:01:06.541
<b>every person is different.</b>

11
00:01:06.541 --> 00:01:09.708
<b>Some individuals are dominated</b>
<b>by certain aspects of nature,</b>

12
00:01:09.708 --> 00:01:13.833
<b>while others are influenced by different aspects.</b>

13
00:01:13.833 --> 00:01:16.916
<b>This can be understood through the perspective</b>

14
00:01:16.916 --> 00:01:21.000
<b>of the Vedic tradition's division of temperaments.</b>

15
00:01:21.000 --> 00:01:22.416
<b>For example,</b>

16
00:01:22.416 --> 00:01:26.708
<b>some are naturally inclined toward strength,</b>

17
00:01:26.708 --> 00:01:28.875
<b>others toward education,</b>

18
00:01:28.875 --> 00:01:31.500
<b>and still others toward business.</b>

19
00:01:31.500 --> 00:01:34.541
<b>At a very surface level, if we wish,</b>

20
00:01:34.541 --> 00:01:38.333
<b>we can understand this classification in </b>
<b>terms of the four ancient categories –</b>

21
00:01:38.333 --> 00:01:39.250
<b>Brahmin,</b>

22
00:01:39.250 --> 00:01:40.208
<b>Kshatriya,</b>

23
00:01:40.208 --> 00:01:41.000
<b>Vaishya,</b>

24
00:01:52.708 --> 00:01:58.625
<b>it would be wrong to expect them </b>
<b>to fight like a warrior on the battlefield.</b>

25
00:01:58.625 --> 00:02:00.958
<b>In previous chapters, Arjuna too</b>

26
00:02:00.958 --> 00:02:06.333
<b>spoke of leaving the war to become </b>
<b>an ascetic, begging like a Brahmin.</b>

27
00:02:06.333 --> 00:02:08.875
<b>Here's a message for him as well –</b>

28
00:02:08.875 --> 00:02:10.125
<b>Arjuna,</b>

29
00:02:10.125 --> 00:02:13.708
<b>if you are a Kshatriya, this is your nature;</b>

30
00:02:13.708 --> 00:02:17.000
<b>begging will feel unnatural,</b>

31
00:02:17.000 --> 00:02:18.375
<b>false to you.</b>

32
00:02:18.375 --> 00:02:19.458
<b>Therefore,</b>

33
00:02:19.458 --> 00:02:23.291
<b>following your warrior's duty is appropriate.</b>

34
00:02:23.291 --> 00:02:27.708
<b>This addresses how our actions align</b>
<b>with our natural tendencies.</b>

35
00:02:27.708 --> 00:02:32.666
<b>However, there's another serious aspect to this...</b>

36
00:02:32.666 --> 00:02:35.958
<b>Someone might mistakenly conclude</b>

37
00:02:35.958 --> 00:02:39.875
<b>that if humans act according </b>
<b>to their natural tendencies,</b>

38
00:02:39.875 --> 00:02:46.208
<b>can they blame their nature </b>
<b>for their sins and misdeeds?</b>

39
00:02:46.208 --> 00:02:47.791
<b>Absolutely not.</b>

40
00:02:47.791 --> 00:02:54.333
<b>Sometimes people give in to their bad </b>
<b>habits formed from old conditioning</b>

41
00:02:54.333 --> 00:02:56.625
<b>and commit unethical acts,</b>

42
00:02:56.625 --> 00:03:00.541
<b>then claim it's just their nature's fault.</b>

43
00:03:00.541 --> 00:03:06.791
<b>Humans have control over whether to apply their </b>
<b>nature toward righteous or unrighteous actions.</b>

44
00:03:06.791 --> 00:03:11.166
<b>To understand this difference, examine </b>
<b>the purpose behind your actions.</b>

45
00:03:11.166 --> 00:03:12.291
<b>Lust,</b>

46
00:03:12.291 --> 00:03:13.291
<b>theft,</b>

47
00:03:13.291 --> 00:03:14.208
<b>violence –</b>

48
00:03:14.208 --> 00:03:17.333
<b>in all these, the doer's intention itself is corrupt.</b>

49
00:03:17.333 --> 00:03:22.625
<b>If your purpose is corrupt,</b>
<b>the responsibility is yours alone.</b>

50
00:03:22.625 --> 00:03:27.166
<b>You must stay away from such </b>
<b>impure thoughts and actions.</b>

51
00:03:27.166 --> 00:03:32.583
<b>A warrior's hands may cause </b>
<b>death on the battlefield,</b>

52
00:03:32.583 --> 00:03:33.583
<b>but</b>

53
00:03:33.583 --> 00:03:37.375
<b>can this be compared to the crime of murder?</b>

54
00:03:37.375 --> 00:03:38.708
<b>Never.</b>

55
00:03:38.708 --> 00:03:42.583
<b>One has the purpose of protecting </b>
<b> country and people,</b>

56
00:03:42.583 --> 00:03:44.750
<b> following the warrior's duty...</b>

57
00:03:44.750 --> 00:03:53.541
<b>while murder is driven by revenge or violence, </b>
<b>which is a poisonous mentality.</b>

58
00:03:53.541 --> 00:03:54.666
<b>Remember,</b>

59
00:03:54.666 --> 00:03:56.875
<b>if someone's purpose is corrupt,</b>

60
00:03:56.875 --> 00:04:00.291
<b>they cannot blame it on their nature –</b>

61
00:04:00.291 --> 00:04:02.500
<b>this is never acceptable.</b>

62
00:04:02.500 --> 00:04:09.708
<b>While living according to their nature, </b>
<b>humans must act righteously.</b>

63
00:04:14.416 --> 00:04:16.833
<b>Everyone has their daily routines</b>

64
00:04:16.833 --> 00:04:18.416
<b>and habits.</b>

65
00:04:18.416 --> 00:04:20.708
<b>Some of these habits are beneficial,</b>

66
00:04:20.708 --> 00:04:25.000
<b>like rising early and exercising,</b>

67
00:04:25.000 --> 00:04:30.625
<b>while others don't serve your best interests,</b>

68
00:04:30.625 --> 00:04:42.000
<b>such as laziness, procrastination, or </b>
<b>spending excessive time on entertainment.</b>

69
00:04:42.000 --> 00:04:46.958
<b>Even knowing that some habits are harmful,</b>

70
00:04:46.958 --> 00:04:50.958
<b>they become difficult to change</b>

71
00:04:50.958 --> 00:04:51.916
<b>because</b>

72
00:04:51.916 --> 00:04:58.875
<b>through constant repetition, these habits </b>
<b>have taken hold of our nature.</b>

73
00:04:58.875 --> 00:05:00.666
<b>This verse explains</b>

74
00:05:00.666 --> 00:05:06.875
<b>that experiencing such tendencies at </b>
<b>different levels is normal for everyone.</b>

75
00:05:06.875 --> 00:05:08.291
<b>However,</b>

76
00:05:08.291 --> 00:05:13.541
<b>when it comes to morality and wrongdoing,</b>

77
00:05:13.541 --> 00:05:18.916
<b>it's crucial to restrain these tendencies.</b>

78
00:05:18.916 --> 00:05:19.916
<b>For instance,</b>

79
00:05:19.916 --> 00:05:27.500
<b>acting out of anger or </b>
<b>dishonesty is never appropriate.</b>

80
00:05:27.500 --> 00:05:32.458
<b>It's natural to feel such </b>
<b>inclinations due to old habits –</b>

81
00:05:32.458 --> 00:05:34.666
<b>there's no fault in that.</b>

82
00:05:34.666 --> 00:05:36.041
<b>But, </b>

83
00:05:36.041 --> 00:05:44.541
<b>the fault lies in transforming these </b>
<b>inclinations and thoughts into actions.</b>

84
00:05:44.541 --> 00:05:46.458
<b>For example,</b>

85
00:05:46.458 --> 00:05:50.541
<b>if a student is unprepared for an exam,</b>

86
00:05:50.541 --> 00:05:51.958
<b>possibly</b>

87
00:05:51.958 --> 00:05:58.541
<b>they might momentarily be tempted to cheat.</b>

88
00:05:58.541 --> 00:06:06.583
<b>But if that student overcomes this thought </b>
<b>and takes the exam with complete integrity,</b>

89
00:06:06.583 --> 00:06:09.875
<b>then even if the results aren't good,</b>

90
00:06:09.875 --> 00:06:15.791
<b>they've certainly passed the test of morality.</b>

91
00:06:15.791 --> 00:06:18.875
<b>Having unethical thoughts isn't wrong –</b>

92
00:06:18.875 --> 00:06:23.250
<b>what's wrong is letting these </b>
<b>thoughts dwell in your mind</b>

93
00:06:23.250 --> 00:06:28.208
<b>and acting unethically under their influence.</b>

94
00:06:28.208 --> 00:06:36.833
<b>This addresses thoughts influenced </b>
<b>by your environment or past conditioning.</b>

95
00:06:36.833 --> 00:06:42.833
<b>Continue your spiritual </b>
<b>progress to keep them pure.</b>

96
00:06:42.833 --> 00:06:44.083
<b>Additionally,</b>

97
00:06:44.083 --> 00:06:51.125
<b>tendencies also refer to the </b>
<b>natural talents within you.</b>

98
00:06:51.125 --> 00:06:52.791
<b>For instance,</b>

99
00:06:52.791 --> 00:06:56.666
<b>some are naturally skilled in sports,</b>

100
00:06:56.666 --> 00:07:00.333
<b>others in art, and others in academics.</b>

101
00:07:00.333 --> 00:07:04.083
<b>Do encourage these tendencies.</b>

102
00:07:04.083 --> 00:07:10.208
<b>Make sure to use them for your life's progress.</b>

103
00:07:10.208 --> 00:07:15.500
<b>The key point is that humans </b>
<b>have three types of tendencies –</b>

104
00:07:15.500 --> 00:07:20.958
<b>some beneficial like your artistic </b>
<b>abilities or exercise habits,</b>

105
00:07:20.958 --> 00:07:24.791
<b>some that hinder progress</b>

106
00:07:24.791 --> 00:07:26.833
<b>like laziness,</b>

107
00:07:26.833 --> 00:07:35.666
<b>and some that are corrupting like deceit.</b>

108
00:07:35.666 --> 00:07:38.666
<b>Encourage good tendencies</b>

109
00:07:38.666 --> 00:07:41.041
<b>Change hindering tendencies</b>

110
00:07:41.041 --> 00:07:45.750
<b>Stay far from corrupting tendencies</b>

111
00:07:45.750 --> 00:07:47.791
<b>In this process,</b>

112
00:07:47.791 --> 00:07:49.291
<b>self-reflection,</b>

113
00:07:49.291 --> 00:07:50.833
<b>spirituality,</b>

114
00:07:50.833 --> 00:07:52.458
<b>and this Gita</b>

115
00:07:52.458 --> 00:07:55.666
<b>will certainly be your guides.</b>

116
00:08:00.375 --> 00:08:05.083
<b>Think of your family as a garden,</b>

117
00:08:05.083 --> 00:08:07.791
<b>where like different plants,</b>

118
00:08:07.791 --> 00:08:09.500
<b>there are many members.</b>

119
00:08:09.500 --> 00:08:12.541
<b>Each member has their unique nature,</b>

120
00:08:12.541 --> 00:08:14.125
<b>special qualities,</b>

121
00:08:14.125 --> 00:08:16.541
<b>and limitations.</b>

122
00:08:16.541 --> 00:08:26.583
<b>Just as different plants need varying amounts </b>
<b>of sunlight, water, and nutrients to develop,</b>

123
00:08:26.583 --> 00:08:28.041
<b>Similarly,</b>

124
00:08:28.041 --> 00:08:34.833
<b>for family members to progress </b>
<b>and flourish according to their capabilities,</b>

125
00:08:34.833 --> 00:08:38.250
<b>they too need different approaches.</b>

126
00:08:38.250 --> 00:08:40.000
<b>For example,</b>

127
00:08:40.000 --> 00:08:43.083
<b>in a family, one child might be sociable,</b>

128
00:08:43.083 --> 00:08:46.208
<b>another brave, another quiet—</b>

129
00:08:46.208 --> 00:08:47.750
<b>similarly,</b>

130
00:08:47.750 --> 00:08:50.875
<b>one might excel in sports,</b>

131
00:08:50.875 --> 00:08:52.041
<b>another in music,</b>

132
00:08:52.041 --> 00:08:54.875
<b>and another in science.</b>

133
00:08:54.875 --> 00:09:02.416
<b>In such cases, expecting everyone </b>
<b>to behave the same way</b>

134
00:09:02.416 --> 00:09:07.708
<b>or progress in the same direction would be wrong.</b>

135
00:09:07.708 --> 00:09:15.083
<b>This would harm their personality </b>
<b>and hinder their development.</b>

136
00:09:15.083 --> 00:09:18.916
<b>This verse states</b>

137
00:09:18.916 --> 00:09:26.708
<b>that all beings operate according </b>
<b>to their qualities and material nature.</b>

138
00:09:26.708 --> 00:09:31.791
<b>Nothing will be achieved </b>
<b>by suppressing this nature.</b>

139
00:09:31.791 --> 00:09:33.625
<b>However,</b>

140
00:09:33.625 --> 00:09:37.125
<b>it's essential to remember</b>

141
00:09:37.125 --> 00:09:40.708
<b>that if someone in the family </b>
<b>has a natural inclination</b>

142
00:09:40.708 --> 00:09:46.125
<b>toward negative behavior or harmful activities,</b>

143
00:09:46.125 --> 00:09:56.125
<b>then in such situations, it's crucial to </b>
<b>guide them wisely toward the right path.</b>

144
00:09:56.125 --> 00:09:59.625
<b>Such situations are easy to identify –</b>

145
00:09:59.625 --> 00:10:00.666
<b>if</b>

146
00:10:00.666 --> 00:10:07.416
<b>someone's nature is causing </b>
<b>harm to themselves or others,</b>

147
00:10:07.416 --> 00:10:13.708
<b>like excessive anger or constant </b>
<b>disrespect of others,</b>

148
00:10:13.708 --> 00:10:18.250
<b>then guidance becomes necessary.</b>

149
00:10:18.250 --> 00:10:19.208
<b>But,</b>

150
00:10:19.208 --> 00:10:28.625
<b>even in such situations, we cannot make the </b>
<b>mistake of declaring them bad or wicked.</b>

151
00:10:28.625 --> 00:10:31.041
<b>The Gita teaches</b>

152
00:10:31.041 --> 00:10:35.750
<b>that every human is fundamentally a soul,</b>

153
00:10:35.750 --> 00:10:40.500
<b>merely acting according to their nature.</b>

154
00:10:40.500 --> 00:10:48.583
<b>Even in adverse circumstances, </b>
<b>they need guidance, not contempt.</b>

155
00:10:48.583 --> 00:10:55.083
<b>When positive tendencies of the young </b>
<b>ones in the family receive encouragement,</b>

156
00:10:55.083 --> 00:11:00.083
<b>and negative tendencies receive guidance,</b>

157
00:11:00.083 --> 00:11:05.791
<b>they will surely become </b>
<b>responsible citizens with age.</b>

158
00:11:05.791 --> 00:11:17.750
<b>A strong and loving family is built on this balance </b>
<b>of acceptance, encouragement, and guidance.</b>

159
00:11:17.750 --> 00:11:19.166
<b>Reflect upon this.</b>

160
00:11:23.958 --> 00:11:26.166
<b>A professional workplace</b>

161
00:11:26.166 --> 00:11:38.666
<b>is a space where people with diverse skills </b>
<b>and personalities unite for a common goal.</b>

162
00:11:38.666 --> 00:11:43.000
<b>To achieve this collective goal, it's essential</b>

163
00:11:43.000 --> 00:11:47.833
<b>that everyone contributes to their full potential.</b>

164
00:11:47.833 --> 00:11:50.041
<b>Now consider,</b>

165
00:11:50.041 --> 00:11:53.291
<b>if a fish were asked to fly,</b>

166
00:11:53.291 --> 00:11:57.166
<b>or a bird to swim,</b>

167
00:11:57.166 --> 00:12:00.791
<b>would they be capable?</b>

168
00:12:00.791 --> 00:12:02.708
<b>No, right?</b>

169
00:12:02.708 --> 00:12:09.583
<b>The key point is that everyone</b>
<b>can work to their full capacity</b>

170
00:12:09.583 --> 00:12:15.916
<b>only when the work aligns with </b>
<b>their characteristics and nature.</b>

171
00:12:15.916 --> 00:12:21.666
<b>This principle must be understood </b>
<b>in the workplace as well.</b>

172
00:12:21.666 --> 00:12:26.333
<b>People will only be able </b>
<b>to work at their full potential</b>

173
00:12:26.333 --> 00:12:33.416
<b>when their responsibilities align with</b>
<b>their tendencies and specialties.</b>

174
00:12:33.416 --> 00:12:35.416
<b>For example,</b>

175
00:12:35.416 --> 00:12:37.416
<b>some excel in leadership,</b>

176
00:12:37.416 --> 00:12:39.416
<b>others in financial management,</b>

177
00:12:39.416 --> 00:12:41.750
<b>and others in customer service.</b>

178
00:12:41.750 --> 00:12:49.625
<b>All colleagues desire to perform </b>
<b>their work smoothly. Everyone is good.</b>

179
00:12:49.625 --> 00:12:52.083
<b>The only requirement is</b>

180
00:12:52.083 --> 00:12:58.875
<b>to recognize their specialty and </b>
<b>assign responsibilities accordingly.</b>

181
00:12:58.875 --> 00:13:00.583
<b>When this happens,</b>

182
00:13:00.583 --> 00:13:03.208
<b>their self-confidence will grow,</b>

183
00:13:03.208 --> 00:13:06.458
<b>they'll be able to show their full potential,</b>

184
00:13:06.458 --> 00:13:09.000
<b>and consequently,</b>

185
00:13:09.000 --> 00:13:12.541
<b>they'll earn others' respect.</b>

186
00:13:12.541 --> 00:13:16.375
<b>Such an organization will not only </b>
<b>be financially successful,</b>

187
00:13:16.375 --> 00:13:22.625
<b>but its environment will also </b>
<b>become positive and respectful.</b>

188
00:13:22.625 --> 00:13:31.041
<b>Humans are emotional beings. </b>
<b>While salary is necessary,</b>

189
00:13:31.041 --> 00:13:31.958
<b>but, </b>

190
00:13:31.958 --> 00:13:40.166
<b>even more necessary is that their </b>
<b>capabilities are recognized and appreciated.</b>

191
00:13:40.166 --> 00:13:43.583
<b>Anyone can provide a salary,</b>

192
00:13:43.583 --> 00:13:47.791
<b>but such an environment will only develop</b>

193
00:13:47.791 --> 00:13:50.416
<b> when you understand people</b>

194
00:13:50.416 --> 00:13:55.708
<b>and assign responsibilities </b>
<b>according to their nature.</b>

195
00:13:55.708 --> 00:13:57.125
<b>Reflect on this.</b>

